::PC_U02_L03_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L03_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.FA.3
Question:
In a polynomial model, which statement best supports the 
{
=A. Use the given interval and key features from the model.#Correct. Polynomial models must be interpreted with constraints and key features.
~B. Ignore the context and use every real number.#This misses real-world restrictions that may limit the model.
~C. Use only the leading coefficient for every question.#The leading coefficient is useful, but it does not answer every modeling question.
~D. Choose the largest number in the problem.#The largest number may not represent the requested feature.
}
